Appendix C: Distributionally Robust MPC with Wasserstein Ambiguity — Full Formulation

C.1 Problem Statement

Consider the stochastic discrete-time system:

x_{k+1} = f(x_k, u_k) + w_k, \quad w_k \sim \mathbb{P}

where $\mathbb{P}$ is unknown but belongs to a Wasserstein ambiguity set $\mathcal{P}_\theta$ centered at empirical distribution $\hat{\mathbb{P}}_N$.

Definition C.1 (Wasserstein Distance). The $p$-Wasserstein distance between two probability measures $\mathbb{Q}_1, \mathbb{Q}_2$ on $\Xi \subseteq \mathbb{R}^d$ with metric $d(\cdot,\cdot)$ is:

W_p(\mathbb{Q}_1, \mathbb{Q}_2) = \left( \inf_{\pi \in \Pi(\mathbb{Q}_1, \mathbb{Q}_2)} \int_{\Xi \times \Xi} d(\xi_1, \xi_2)^p d\pi(\xi_1, \xi_2) \right)^{1/p}

where $\Pi$ is the set of joint distributions with marginals $\mathbb{Q}_1, \mathbb{Q}_2$.

Ambiguity Set:
\mathcal{P}_\theta = \{\mathbb{Q} \in \mathcal{M}(\Xi) : W_p(\mathbb{Q}, \hat{\mathbb{P}}_N) \leq \theta\}

The radius $\theta$ is selected to guarantee $\mathbb{P} \in \mathcal{P}_\theta$ with confidence $1-\beta$:

\theta(\beta, N) = C \cdot \left(\frac{\log(1/\beta)}{N}\right)^{1/\max(d,2)}

where $C$ depends on the diameter of support $\Xi$. (Mohajerin Esfahani & Kuhn, 2018)

C.2 DR-CVaR Reformulation

The DR-CVaR constraint:

\sup_{\mathbb{Q} \in \mathcal{P}_\theta} \text{CVaR}_\alpha^{\mathbb{Q}}(\ell(x,u,w)) \leq 0

is equivalent to the existence of $\lambda \geq 0, \tau \in \mathbb{R}$ such that:

\lambda \theta + \frac{1}{N} \sum_{i=1}^N \left[ \tau + \frac{1}{1-\alpha} (\ell(x,u,\hat{w}^{(i)}) - \tau - \lambda d(\hat{w}^{(i)}, w)_+ \right] \leq 0

where $(\cdot)_+ = \max(\cdot, 0)$.

For the special case of $d(w, \hat{w}) = \|w - \hat{w}\|_2$, this becomes a tractable convex constraint when $\ell$ is convex in $w$.

C.3 DRO-MPC Finite-Horizon Optimization

At each MPC step, we solve:

\begin{aligned}
\min_{\mathbf{u}, \mathbf{x}} \quad & \sum_{k=0}^{H-1} \ell_{\text{stage}}(x_k, u_k) + V_f(x_H) \\
\text{s.t.} \quad & x_{k+1} = f(x_k, u_k), \quad x_0 = x_{\text{current}} \\
& x_k \in \mathcal{X}, \quad u_k \in \mathcal{U} \\
& \exists \lambda_k \geq 0, \tau_k: \lambda_k \theta + \frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^N \left[ \tau_k + \frac{(g(x_k, u_k, \hat{w}^{(i)}) - \tau_k)_+}{1-\alpha} \right] \leq 0 \\
& \forall k = 0,\ldots,H-1
\end{aligned}

where $g(\cdot)$ encodes collision avoidance or other safety constraints.

C.4 Asynchronous Update with Event Trigger

The risk-monitor thread (Algorithm C.1) updates $\beta$ and $\theta$ only when the state covariance $\Sigma_t$ exceeds thresholds. The MPC uses the last updated values with a timestamp check.

Algorithm C.1: Event-Triggered Risk Monitor

